    "text": "Tech Stocks\nOracle’s stock is seeing its worst run in a quarter-century as this key AI debate rages on\nWhile Oracle’s cloud-infrastructure business is growing rapidly, a massive $95 billion spending plan and a physical bottleneck in data-center deliveries are giving investors pause\nShares of Oracle moved sharply lower Thursday, showcasing Wall Street’s negative reaction to the company’s latest earnings report.\nWhile Oracle ORCL beat the revenue and earnings benchmarks set by analysts, the stock fell 8.5% as investors wrestle with a crucial uncertainty: Can Oracle convert its artificial-intelligence backlog into actual revenue?",
